0.0,"_gate_piotroski":5,"_gp_piotroski":false,"_score_piotroski":55.6,"_gate_spread":0.0573190098085007,"_gp_spread":false,"_score_spread":28.7,"_gate_roic_consistency":0.7220217238223776,"_gp_roic_consistency":false,"_score_roic_consistency":0.0,"_gate_incr_roic":0.0007464636285596984,"_gp_incr_roic":false,"_score_incr_roic":16.9,"_gate_margin_advantage":0.30126409731618753,"_gp_margin_advantage":true,"_score_margin_advantage":100.0,"_gate_pool_share":null,"_gp_pool_share":null,"_score_pool_share":null,"_gate_rev_durability":0.33872730287033526,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":100.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":0.04203111552536809,"_gp_fcf_durability":false,"_score_fcf_durability":46.0,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":0.0,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.09143853849112618,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":100.0,"_gate_share_shrink":-0.0013442982624055633,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":51.7,"_gate_sbc_dilution":null,"_gp_sbc_dilution":null,"_score_sbc_dilution":0.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.64079005,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":100.0,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"MPLX LP owns and operates midstream energy infrastructure and logistics assets primarily in the United States. It operates in two segments, Crude Oil and Products Logistics; and Natural Gas and NGL Services. The company is involved in the gathering, processing, and transportation of natural gas; gathering, transportation, fractionation, storage, and marketing of natural gas liquids; gathering, storage, transportation, and distribution of crude oil and refined products, as well as other hydrocarbon-based products and renewables; and sale of residue gas and condensate. It also engages in inland marine businesses, comprising fleet of boats and barges transport light products, heavy oils, crude oil, renewable fuels, chemicals, and feedstocks in the Mid-Continent and Gulf Coast regions, as well as a marine repair facility located on the Ohio River; and distribution of fuel, as well as operates refining logistics, terminals, rail facilities, and storage caverns. In addition, it operates terminal facilities for the receipt, storage, blending, additization, handling, and redelivery of refined petroleum products through the pipeline, rail, marine, and truck transportation. MPLX GP LLC acts as the general partner of MPLX LP. The company was incorporated in 2012 and is headquartered in Findlay, Ohio. MPLX LP operates as a subsidiary of Marathon Petroleum Corporation.","ceo_bio":"Ms. Maryann T. Mannen | President, CEO & Chairman of the Board of MPLX GP LLC | Age 62 | Compensation: $5.2M (FY2025)","financial_summary":["MPLX LP is a large-cap energy business with a $58.0B market cap on $13.0B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +4% over the past three years and +34% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory. Operating margins are contracting by -11.7pp, the first warning that competitive pressure is eroding the franchise.","Returns on capital run at 14% against a 8% cost of capital, a 6-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it.","The business throws off $4.1B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 32 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.20\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 4.0\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and interest coverage runs at 6.0\u00d7.","Management returns a meaningful 9.1% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 64% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and within its sector the business captures 4.2\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Operating margins contracting -11.7pp YoY \u2014 competitive pressure is eroding the franchise","sev":"red","cat":"trend"},{"text":"Payout ratio looks stretched \u2014 the dividend\u2019s own margin of safety is thin","sev":"red","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"Carries a 93% premium to sector median EV/EBITDA (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.9250071694866648},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"The commodity cycle \u2014 revenue and free cash flow are ultimately hostage to a price the company does not set, and the long-run energy-transition arc adds a structural overhang.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"ESG-driven capital flight and stranded asset risk \u2014 tightening climate policy and investor mandates raise the cost of capital and risk leaving reserves permanently in the ground.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Geopolitical supply shocks \u2014 wars, sanctions, and OPEC decisions create volatility that no hedging programme can fully neutralise.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 30% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","13 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Energy sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter","Energy ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Quarterly Earnings Drop Might Change The Case For Investing In MPLX (MPLX)","source":"simplywall.st","l